    "summary": "From delving into design history and creative theory to exploring materials, colour and light, entrepreneurship and digital integration, this DIA-recognised course will equip you with the skills and knowledge to conquer interior design. Our ethical design philosophy has a strong focus on designing for humanity and positive social outcomes, with the opportunity to work on live projects with NFPs and charitable organisations. We also take a sustainable design approach, ensuring that our practices and thinking throughout the course are explored with the environment in mind. Thanks to our in-depth industry partnerships, you'll have the chance to dive into real-world business experiences and secure placements that open doors to invaluable industry connections. Upon completion of the Bachelor degree, you will also be eligible to join the Design Institute of Australia and apply for the GOTYA (Graduate of the Year Awards). Throughout the degree, you will: Immerse yourself in design culture, delving deep into the nuances of creative theory and history. Translate theory into practice by honing your practical skills in creative interior design and the art of conceptualisation. Gain valuable hands-on experience in design technologies, events, and installations. Collaborate on real industry projects alongside seasoned interior designers and influential brand leaders. Learn interior design practices and entrepreneurship, acquiring knowledge and experience that will set you apart from the competition. Craft a standout portfolio featuring a collection of creative projects that exhibit innovation and showcase your unique talents. Design innovative interiors by applying creative methodologies, taking creative risks and reflecting critically on your work and ideas. Work with mentors and cross-collaborate with students from other Collarts courses. Interpret design briefs to meet the needs of clients and create designs that are relevant and fit for purpose. Develop design approaches that are environmentally responsible and created with social connection, accessibility and cultural inclusivity in mind.",
