    "summary": "This is a blend of the Bachelor of Design (Fashion & Sustainability) and the Bachelor of Applied Business (Fashion Marketing). It’s a carefully curated balance of contemporary garment design, sustainable construction methods, and the business savvy and ethics required for the fashion world – both now and in the future. If your aspirations lean towards becoming a Fashion Brand or Marketing Manager, Social Media or E-commerce Guru, Visual Merchandiser, Fashion Buyer or Merchandiser, Stylist, Public Relations Luminary, or even a Creative Director, then this Double Degree is your ultimate pathway. Your education won't just be theoretical; it will be a hands-on experience guided by industry experts shaping the sustainable fashion landscape within major brands, fashion houses, and top-tier agencies. Begin with Fashion & Sustainability, and then seamlessly transition into the second degree, selecting units from Buying & Retail Management and Branding & Communications to tailor your learning. Throughout the double degree, you will: Gain an in-depth understanding of fashion business, marketing, publicity, entrepreneurship, branding, and social media. Learn practical skills in fashion merchandising, styling, trend forecasting, sustainable design, and ethical production practices. Create, develop, and produce ethical fashion products and services with a strong focus on sustainability and innovation. Acquire knowledge and experience in global fashion practices, ethical responsibility, circular fashion systems, and zero-waste techniques and technologies. Employ creative, technical, business, and communication skills across fashion design, marketing, retail, branding, and digital content creation. Work on industry projects with fashion designers, brands, and creative professionals in real-world environments. Gain hands-on experience through fashion shows, installations, gallery events, industry placements, and opportunities with Melbourne Fashion Week, Fashion Revolution, Ego Expo, and more. Develop an industry-relevant portfolio and capstone project showcasing both creative and strategic fashion expertise. Participate in international exchange opportunities and collaborative projects with students across creative disciplines. Study on-campus or blended, with access to Collarts’ creative learning spaces, industry-led teaching, and professional facilities.",
