    "summary": "A Diploma of Design in Fashion & Sustainability from Collarts is where creativity meets conscious design. Led by industry experts who are at the forefront of sustainable fashion design, reinvention, forecasting, and enterprise, you’ll gain the creative and technical skills to design ethically and sustainably in today’s ever evolving fashion landscape. With the flexibility of a Diploma, you can learn in a way that suits you, whether it’s on campus or online. You’ll learn the foundations of fashion design, sketching, and technical drawing, while exploring fibres, fabrics, and the environmental impact of material choices. Attain insights into sustainable business models, transparent supply chains, and how circular, recycled, and low-impact systems shape the future of the industry. Experiment with garment reinvention, and lifecycle extension through hands-on construction and digital design tools. With industry awareness built into the course, you’ll engage with real creative environments, and graduate prepared to contribute to innovative, ethical, and sustainable fashion practices. Throughout the degree, you will: Develop broad and coherent knowledge of sustainable fashion design, ethical practices, material innovation, and the social and environmental impact of the fashion industry. Utilise theoretical, practical, and creative knowledge to enter the fashion industry at an introductory level. Analyse information from a range of sources to evaluate approaches to unpredictable problems and changing contexts in contemporary fashion practice. Employ cognitive, technical, and communication skills across fashion design, garment construction, digital design tools, and sustainable production practices. Communicate key specialist knowledge of fashion and sustainability as a basis for collaboration, innovation, and industry engagement. Exercise initiative and judgement in decision-making and planning for fashion design projects and sustainable creative outcomes. Work autonomously on fashion projects with responsibility and accountability for your own outputs in independent or collaborative situations. Gain hands-on experience through practical design projects and engagement with real creative environments. Collaborate on industry-focused projects with students from other creative disciplines. Study on-campus or online with access to Collarts’ creative learning resources and industry-informed teaching.",
