    "intake": "2026-07-13",
    "prerequisites": "Applicants who successfully complete the EmpowerED University Preparation Program with a GPA of 4 or above, will be eligible for guaranteed admission* into a range of Griffith degrees. *Guaranteed admission applies to rank only. Applicants must still meet all other requirements for admission such as additional prerequisites. For further details visit EmpowerED University Preparation Program .",
    "assumed": "Not listed by UAC.",
    "additionalCriteria": "",
    "fees": "Refer to Griffith University current fee information .",
    "summary": "The EmpowerED University Preparation Program provides a pathway for applicants who don't meet the formal admission requirements to enter an undergraduate degree at Griffith University. This free, comprehensive preparatory program, gives you the opportunity to experience university life while building your confidence and academic study skills. You'll gain fundamental knowledge and skills - including the essentials of critical reading, writing and referencing - in a supportive learning environment. Note: Students currently enrolled in Year 12 are not eligible for admission. This program is offered full-time and part-time at the Gold Coast and Logan campuses. Courses are also available online. Each course is delivered in a 6 week block model with two, three-hour workshops per week. Students will complete the program full-time from January to June or July to December.",
    "careers": "You'll be set up for success through courses covering university preparation, academic study skills, communication and academic research, and mathematics essentials. You'll even be able to start shaping your future career now with a personalised employability plan.",
