    "summary": "The Bachelor of Clinical Science is your fast track into the Doctor of Physiotherapy. By taking advantage of an intensive summer session, you’ll complete your undergraduate degree in just two years. Then, if you meet the entry requirements, you’ll receive direct entry into the Doctor of Physiotherapy, which will qualify you to work as a practicing physiotherapist. The Doctor of Physiotherapy –the first three-year master-level professional-entry physiotherapy degree in New South Wales – will develop your skills so that when you graduate you’re able to work with individuals across the lifespan to optimise their physical function. You’ll learn to effectively assess, diagnose and treat individuals with a range of health conditions. You’ll also learn how to encourage people to change their behaviour and self-manage their conditions to maximise their physical health. To progress from the Bachelor of Clinical Science to the Doctor of Physiotherapy, you will need to meet all of the following conditions: (1) successfully complete your Bachelor degree; (2) achieve a minimum Weighted Average Mark of 65 in your Bachelor degree; (3) achieve a satisfactory Casper test score completed within the 12 months prior to commencement date of the Doctor of Physiotherapy degree; (4) commence your postgraduate degree within 10 years of completing your Bachelor degree.",
