    "summary": "This course provides a comprehensive foundation in the breadth of business disciplines before students proceed to the in-depth study of the chosen major field of specialisation: accounting, management, marketing, and digital marketing. As well as a range of core units, students can also broaden their degree through a range of interesting and relevant electives. All Bachelor of Business students participate for course credit in an online-simulated business venture competition against 600 other universities worldwide. In addition to teaching the body of theory and developing students' technical skills, lecturers provide students with a variety of course work to give them scope to develop the MIT graduate attributes. These include critical skills in communication and analysis, cultural awareness and a commitment to ethical standards in the global context, which contribute to well-rounded graduates who are work-ready and able to add value to employers in any location worldwide. MIT Sydney graduates are equipped to stay up-to-date in knowledge and skills, and are commercially valuable professionals in accounting, management, marketing or digital marketing in the global market.",
