    "summary": "The Advanced Diploma of Interior Design and Decoration, built in response to changing industry standards is your ticket to a career as a professional in the field. This course arms you with the skills to gain industry recognition as an Interior Designer creating innovative spaces that stand out. Whether you’re creating from the ground up, revamping residential spaces or taking on new commercial projects, you’ll learn to fuse style, comfort and sustainability. Learning outcomes: Learn essential skills in creating decorative schemes, furnishings, and finishes, integrating efficiency, comfort, and sustainability in your designs. Concept and produce innovative floor plans, sections, elevations, 2D technical drawings and 3D models at a professional level. Get to grips with industry-standard software and design tools AutoCAD and SketchUp Pro, used by designers across the globe. Complete a Capstone Project where you’ll develop your professional identity, analyse a commercial project brief, conduct project research and generate design themes and concepts. Develop awareness of the legislation and frameworks within the industry able to protect your business and the spaces of those you create for. Undertake 120 hours of experience by completing an internship or working on a live brief.",
    "careers": "Interior designer, interior stylist, real estate home stager, materials and furnishing consultant.",
    "practicalExperience": "120 hours of real-world experience during your course. You can choose between an internship or an industry live brief, in addition to completing a double capstone project.",
