    "summary": "The Bachelor of Primary Education provides the academic skills you need to support, engage and extend primary-aged children by integrating theory and practice. The Bachelor of Primary Education focuses on the characteristics, development and needs of primary school children and the knowledge, skills and experience you will need to teach them at an excellent standard. Courses focus on the key learning areas (school subjects) in the primary curriculum – English and Literacy, Mathematics and Numeracy, Science and Technology, Health and Physical Education, the arts and the social sciences. You will complete 30 weeks (150 days) of professional experience placements in schools, building your skills and confidence to enter the profession that changes the lives of the next generation. You can select a specialisation in religious education, which will make you eligible for accreditation to teach in Catholic schools, or in English education, mathematics education or special and inclusive education.",
