    "summary": "The Bachelor of Accounting is a specialist degree for high-achieving students who view an accounting career as an excellent foundation for future business leaders. All students in the course receive a scholarship package over three years and undertake a year of full-time industry internships. They are encouraged to complete a second major or sub-major in another business discipline. The course has a graduate employment rate greater than 95 per cent. If you are interested in Accounting, you can also list 601030 Bachelor of Business (FT) as a preference. For further information, visit the UTS Business School website .",
