    "summary": "The Bachelor of Communication in Digital and Social Media at UTS is designed to keep you up to date with the latest industry trends and provide you with practical, hands-on experience underpinned by applied academic research. You’ll acquire essential skills in social media communication, user experience and app design, and data analysis and visualisation. Students engage with real-world scenarios and contemporary debates in digital and social media, develop innovative and impactful strategies, and examine the societal impacts of digital technology, including AI and data bias, ethical implications of technology, and technology’s role in solving problems and improving lives. Collaborative learning in this course provides opportunities to work in transdisciplinary teams on industry-based projects, building a professional portfolio that showcases your skills to potential employers. This course prepares you for the current job market and instils an awareness of the broader implications of digital technologies and their potential to drive positive social change. Upon completion, you’ll be a versatile digital media professional, ready to tackle the challenges of today's tech-driven world with critical thinking, ethical awareness, and practical expertise. To increase your career flexibility, you can add a second stream from five of the other streams offered in the Bachelor of Communication, and build further skills and portfolios that equip you for a range of work options in media and communication. These courses give you practical and transferrable skills for the expanding media industries.",
    "careers": "Social media manager, UX/UI designer, digital campaign manager, prototype designer, digital entrepreneur, policy analyst, digital content producer, digital marketing specialist, communications officer.",
