    "summary": "The Bachelor of Fashion Business is a future-focused, interdisciplinary course to prepare you for diverse careers in the dynamic and evolving global fashion industry. In this innovative undergraduate program, you will gain the business acumen and industry insight required to navigate and lead in contemporary fashion business environments. Drawing on the combined strengths of the School of Design and the UTS Business School, the course offers you a unique learning experience that integrates core business disciplines such as economics, finance, accounting, marketing, and management underpinned by a deep understanding of fashion as a cultural and social phenomenon. This course distinguishes itself by embedding sustainability and business ethics through a systems-thinking approach. You will critically engage with the fashion industry’s challenges and opportunities, developing a holistic perspective on responsible fashion business practice. You will study alongside peers in related disciplines, fostering cross-disciplinary collaboration and innovation. By the time you graduate, you will be equipped with the skills and knowledge to drive sustainable and ethical change across various fashion business contexts from brand management and retail strategy to product development and supply chain operations.",
