    "summary": "A Bachelor of Laws from UOW equips graduates with a comprehensive legal education; a world-class degree that provides a thorough grounding in the law, as well as a real-world focus on the essential practical skills and the commercial, social and ethical context in which the law operates. The UOW Law First Year Program provides all first-year students with the support of a First Year Coordinator and the POD (small group) experience, in which students remain in the same tutorial group across all four first semester subjects. The Bachelor of Laws (Graduate Entry) is a three-year full-time degree (or can be studied part-time) which covers the prescribed areas of knowledge for future admission to the profession and includes a choice of electives. Additionally, an integrated skills program equips graduates with experience in areas such as legal research, interviewing, legal writing, advocacy and negotiation. Opportunities also exist to undertake subjects through an international exchange program. We believe that practical experience is a vital part of your legal training and are the only law school in New South Wales that requires you to complete a legal internship. The Bachelor of Laws at UOW covers all the core law areas and includes cutting-edge electives in sustainability, artificial intelligence and international law. You may also wish to consider studying honours as part of your Bachelor of Laws.",
