    "summary": "Prepare for a meaningful career in health, physical education, and sport. You’ll study across four key areas: health education, physical education, sport, and movement science. Together, these areas of study give you the knowledge, skills, and vision to lead quality health and physical education – contributing to the health and wellbeing of all young people; reimagine sport – making it inclusive, innovate, and for everyone; and have in-depth content knowledge applicable to health and movement science (HMS), sport, leisure, and recreation (SLR), and physical activity and sport studies (PASS). With eight flexible subjects, you’ll also get to shape your learning, and your future career opportunities, with options in sport and event management, psychology and wellbeing, education, and health promotion. With a strong focus on young people, you’ll build contemporary health knowledge and the confidence to lead informed conversations around important and emerging health issues – supporting positive decision-making. You’ll also develop movement expertise and practical teaching capabilities, equipping you to design and deliver engaging physical education experiences that foster lifelong participation in physical activity. Across the degree, there is a strong emphasis on rethinking sport and physical activity to be more inclusive, creative, and accessible, enabling you to make a meaningful impact across schools, clubs, and communities.",
