    "campus": "Parramatta campus",
    "campusCode": "PA",
    "campusPostcode": "2116",
    "area": "Evidence-based midwifery, midwifery knowledge and skills, woman-centred care, primary health care.",
    "courseLevel": "TBP",
    "atar": "78.50",
    "atarYear": 2025,
    "duration": "3 years full-time",
    "modes": [
      "On campus",
      "Full-time"
    ],
    "intake": "2027-03-01",
    "prerequisites": "Refer to Western Sydney University general admission criteria.",
    "assumed": "Not listed by UAC.",
    "additionalCriteria": "Refer to Western Sydney University general admission criteria.",
    "fees": "Refer to Western Sydney University current fee information .",
    "summary": "Do you want to be a skilled and caring midwife with the expertise to support women and their families during pregnancy, birth and beyond? This program offers theoretical knowledge, simulated experiences and Midwifery Practice Experience (MPE) that enables students to develop the necessary skills to provide safe and effective woman-centred midwifery care. Prospective students should be familiar with the inherent requirements of the program and be aware that impairment that may detrimentally impact on your practice will need to be disclosed when applying for registration as a midwife. Additionally, there is a requirement to declare any criminal history. Deferment for this program is not available. All applicants will be required to declare how they meet the English Language Proficiency requirement or complete an English language test with an IELTS proficiency of 7.0 overall and in all bands (or equivalent) prior to being made an offer. Applicants are advised to check the English Language Proficiency (ELP) requirements on the Nursing and Midwifery Board of Australia website. The Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (AHPRA) has a register of students enrolled in the Bachelor of Midwifery for the duration of their study. Western Sydney University as the education provider, will provide your details directly to the Nursing and Midwifery Board of Australia (NMBA) for registration while you are a student.",
    "careers": "Work in midwifery group practice, team midwifery, caseload midwifery, homebirth, birth centres, antenatal clinics, postnatal wards, birthing units, postnatal clinics, community midwifery services, research, management, teaching and policy development.",
    "practicalExperience": "Midwifery Practice Experience (MPE) at a home hospital is integrated throughout the program in addition to the home hospital, students gain experience in other midwifery-related areas in the community. Students learn to provide effective woman-centred care by working in partnership with women and their families during their pregnancy, labour and birth and the early post-birth period. Midwifery Practice Experience occurs across the calendar year. Students are advised that any break in study may impact on their home hospital experience.",
    "uacUrl": "https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/726570",
    "officialUrl": "https://www.westernsydney.edu.au/future/study/courses/undergraduate/bachelor-of-midwifery",
    "source": "UAC Course Search undergraduate API, imported 2026-06-17",
    "dedupedCount": 1
