    "area": "In addition to science subject areas in chemistry, biodiversity and cell biology, the double major will cover areas in human-animal interactions, wildlife studies, animal nutrition and feeding, animal reproduction, animal health and welfare, vertebrate and invertebrate zoology, ecology, comparative physiology and research. You will have options to undertake subjects in non-science disciplines including Business, law and language to expand your employment opportunities.",
