    "assumed": "At least two of Biology, Chemistry, Mathematics Advanced, Physics. Students who have not undertaken HSC-level mathematics, or have attempted Mathematics Standard 2 or Mathematics Advanced but achieved no higher than Band 2 or 3, may be required to take a study pattern that includes preparatory studies in mathematics in readiness for the higher level mathematics required in this program. Refer to Western Sydney University general admission criteria .",
    "additionalCriteria": "",
    "fees": "Refer to Western Sydney University current fee information .",
    "summary": "Study Food Science and Innovation at Western Sydney University and prepare for a journey of discovery. This program will equip you to lead the development of new, safe, healthy, and sustainable foods. You will gain a solid foundation in biological and chemical sciences, providing you with the applied knowledge and skills necessary for a career in the food industry, one of the world's largest business sectors. You can also choose to major in Human Nutrition, delving into food and nutrient concepts related to human metabolism and physiology, as well as the management of nutrients in relation to appetite, exercise, health, and disease. Additionally, you will develop a wide range of laboratory and research skills. Our program has strong connections with industry and the community, offering access to modern sensory, food processing pilot plant, and kitchen facilities at Hawkesbury Campus. You'll also have the opportunity to undertake work placements and research alongside our experienced staff.",
    "careers": "Food scientist, food researcher, secondary school teacher, product developer, food quality assurance officer, food safety professional, food production management, food chemist, food sensory evaluation, consumer relations, food marketing.",
    "practicalExperience": "",
    "uacUrl": "https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/728187",
