    "additionalCriteria": "",
    "fees": "Refer to Western Sydney University current fee information .",
    "summary": "Become a hands-on environmental problem-solver. Dive into fieldwork and immerse yourself in our cutting-edge labs at the Western Sydney University Hawkesbury campus. You will learn from renowned experts in fields such as ecology, climate science, and conservation, while also gaining hands-on skills in data analysis, project management, and community engagement. Our program emphasizes experiential learning, with citizen science and strong industry partnerships that enable you to make a real-world impact. By focusing on problem-solving and critical thinking, we prepare you to address complex environmental challenges and contribute to building a sustainable future.",
    "careers": "Graduates can expect careers as environmental officers in local and state government agencies, work with industry as environmental consultants or engage in biological conservation.",
