    "summary": "Want to give yourself the best possible chance to get into a Nursing, Midwifery or Health Science degree at Western? The Undergraduate Preparation Program in Nursing/Health Science will set you on a path for success in your future studies. This tuition-free program offers personalised support, practical learning experiences, and a strong foundation for university success. Modular learning: This program is delivered through modular learning , helping you reach your potential, no matter your starting point or ATAR. You'll study one course-specific subject a time. What pathways to further study does this program provide? Upon successful completion of this Undergraduate Preparation Program you can transition into the first year of study of: Diploma of Health Science Bachelor of Health Science (minimum grade point average required) Bachelor of Nursing (minimum grade point average required)* Bachelor of Midwifery (minimum grade point average required)* *Additional English language proficiency requirements set by the Australian Nursing and Midwifery Accreditation Council (ANMAC) must be declared and met before students are eligible to commence study in the Bachelor of Nursing or Bachelor of Midwifery at Western Sydney University.",
